{
    "background_story": "Jeremiah was a notorious pirate captain who roamed the Caribbean seas, striking fear into the hearts of his enemies. He earned the nickname 'Blackheart' for his ruthless tactics and ability to evade capture. Jeremiah's ship, the 'Maverick's Revenge', was a symbol of his rogue spirit, with its black sails and hull adorned with the skulls of his vanquished foes. He had no allegiance to any nation or code, answering only to his own sense of justice. Jeremiah's exploits became the stuff of legend, with tales of his daring heists and narrow escapes from the authorities. Despite his fearsome reputation, he had a soft spot for the downtrodden and often targeted the ships of corrupt merchants and tyrannical rulers. Jeremiah's rogue nature made him a hero to some and a villain to others, but one thing was certain: he lived life on his own terms.",
